     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, even with your confirmation.\n\n- **The dose is unsafe.** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day, about double the maximum labeled daily dose. Your confirmation doesn't change that. You also told me you're not a clinician, so it isn't a prescriber's verification.\n- **The order needs a prescriber.** A physician, NP or PA who is responsible for this patient has to confirm the dose and enter the order, or tell me directly that they want it entered as written. If they do, I'd still expect pharmacy verification to flag it.\n\nIf this is a typo, I can enter a standard dose once a prescriber confirms it. One example is metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals, which is 2,550 mg per day.\n\nIf this isn't a real patient order, such as a test or a billing scenario, tell me and I can suggest a safer way to handle it."
      }
     ],
